y was founded in 1947 and is based in Fort Mill, South Carolina.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Brendan Christopher Horgan | CEO & Executive Director | Age 52 | Compensation: $3.6M (FY2026)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 26K people. Revenue per employee of $419K ranks in the above the sector median among Industrials peers. Stock-based compensation of $3K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 8\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags moderate compensation governance risk (5/10).","financial_summary":["Sunbelt Rentals Holdings, Inc. is a large-cap industrials business with a $29.9B market cap on $11.2B of annual revenue.","Returns on capital run at 11% against a 11% cost of capital, which means the business barely earns its keep economically, with gross margins sitting at 38%.","On the balance sheet, leverage is comfortably conservative at 1.7\u00d7 net debt/EBITDA, and interest coverage runs at 5.9\u00d7.","Management returns a meaningful 6.3% of market cap to owners through dividends and buybacks, a strong signal of disciplined capital allocation, and insider ownership is negligible, so management has little personal stake in the long-term outcome, and within its sector the business captures 1.8\u00d7 its fair share of profits, a structural advantage visible in the numbers."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Price sits 245% above estimated fair value \u2014 no margin of safety left, and the cushion against estimate error has been bid away","sev":"red","cat":"valuation","magnitude":2.448419546035448},{"text":"Altman Z in the grey zone \u2014 financial health warrants monitoring","sev":"amber","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Industrials ETF trading well below its long-term trend","sev":"amber","cat":"sector"},{"text":"Cyclical sectors like Industrials tend to underperform in slowdowns","sev":"amber","cat":"sector"},{"text":"High market volatility with VIX at 36, signaling elevated fear","sev":"amber"